1 NOTE Became a Spanish judge and governor of New Spain from July 4, 1526 to July 16, 1526.
2 CONT Became a knight of Cordoba.
2 CONT In the year of 1525 King Charles appointed Luis Ponce de Leon as Judge of the residence and governor of New Spain.
2 CONT He sailed from San Lucar de Barrameda on Feb 2, 1526. He then was detained in Hispanola until May 31, 1526 to get his ship repaired. He finally arrived in Mexico City and presented himself to the city government, (Ayuntamiento.) H
2 CONC e had the decree from Toledo dated Nov 4, 1525 granting him governorship. At this time he was 65 Years of age, ill with a fever he had gotten on his arrival at Veracruz. He was sick during the twelve day journey to the capital. he
2 CONC  died soon after.
2 CONT His brother, Juan Ponce de Leon, the discoverer of La Florida had died in 1521.
2 CONT Archiv. Seccion Noblez del Archivo Historico Nacional
2 CONT Sig: Ocuna,C.117,D.13
