3 TEXT 87. Antão Gonçalves de Ávila (João Bethencourt, Georges, Regnault, Jean, Jean, Jean, Regnault, Philippe, Jean)434,251,6,7,9,435,256,55,6,7,9,435,256,55,6,7,9 was also known as Antão Gonçalves d'Ávila Betencourt.55 He was also know
4 CONC n as Antão Gonçalvez de Avilla.435 He was born circa 1440 at Castile.257,6,9 He married Dona Inês Gonçalves de Antona, daughter of Afonso Gonçalves de Antona and Ignes Rodrigues Fagundes, at Graciosa (Os Bettencourt gives the loca
4 CONC tion of the marriage as Graçiosa, adding that the bride brought, as her dowry, lands which her father possessed there, but the Nobiliário de Famílias de Portugal gives the location as Villa de Praia, Terceira).435,6,7,9,28,434 He 
4 CONC and Dona Inês Gonçalves de Antona had seven children.436 He and Dona Inês Gonçalves de Antona resided at Praia da Vitória, Terceira.436 Antão Gonçalves de Ávila and João Sanchez Gonçalves de Ávila came to live in Terceira, being C
4 CONC astilian, to become one of those who followed the Comunidades in the time of Emperor Charles V.344,345 Emperor Charles V reigned between 1519 and 1558 at the Holy Roman Empire.346This branch came from Spain to Almeida and then to 
4 CONC the Açores, establishing themselves on Terceira when it was under Castilian domination.251,57
