1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Fernando de Toledo Oropesa was born in Spain in 1520, the son of Luis de Toledo y Pacheco and Inés Duque Estrada.[1] A noble family, they were related to the counts of Oropesa and to Cardinal Juan Álvarez de Toledo
2 CONC .[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He studied at the University of Salamanca.[1] While there, he became friends with Juan de Ribera.[1] After university, he was ordained as a priest.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT The King of Spain offered him several ecclesiastical posts, but Toledo refused them all.[1] He was appointed president of the Royal Audiencia of Lima; he initially accepted this position, but then reconsidered and declined to trav
2 CONC el to the Viceroyalty of Peru.[1] Instead, he remained in Spain and dedicated himself to preaching, hearing confessions, and assisting the sick and poor.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon the insistence of Philip II of Spain, Pope Gregory XIII made him a cardinal in the consistory of February 21, 1578.[1] The nuncio in Spain, Cardinal Filippo Sega communicated the king's thanks to the pope on March 13, 1578, b
2 CONC ut then on May 5 reported that Toledo had declined the appointment.[1] The pope and the king agreed that Sega could convey the biretta to Toledo on the assumption that Toledo could be prevailed upon to accept the appointment.[1] H
2 CONC owever, Toledo refused repeatedly and on July 4, 1578, the pope accepted Toledo's refusal and withdrew his creation, complaining to Philip II that the king had insisted he make a cardinal of someone who would refuse the honor.[1] 
2 CONC The king replied that he never imagined any of his subjects would refuse a cardinalate.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Toledo continued his priestly duties until his death.[1] He died in Oropesa in 1590, in the middle of giving a sermon. He was buried in the monastery of the Immaculate Conception in Oropesa.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Entry from Biographical Dictionary of the Cardinals of the Holy Roman Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Toledo de Oropesa, Fernando de (1520-1590) Fuentes:	Papeles varios políticos (Mss/18434); h. 5 (Don Fernando de Toledo, hermano del Conde de Oropesa) WWW catholic-hierarchy.org 28-01-2012; (Padre Fernando de Toledo de Oropesa; nom
2 CONC brado Cardenal en 1578, renunció)
2 CONT
