1 OCCU Beatrix Pacheco was lady-in-waiting of Queen Eleanore, wife ofKing François I, and daughter of the Duke of Escalona (sic. ed: actually great-granddaughter of the past duque).
1 TITL Countess
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Beatrix Pacheco was lady-in-waiting of Queen Eleanore, wife of King François I, and daughter of the Duke of Escalona (sic. ed: actually great- granddaughter of the past duque).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/261544291/beatrice-de_montbel_d'entremont
2 CONT
2 CONT Dates approx. Beatrice (Béatrix) Pacheco was Countess of Entremont and Dame de Montbel.
2 CONT
2 CONT She met Sébastien, Count of Entremont and Montbel in Paris and they married on 17 September 1539 in the presence of the Dauphin (the future Henry II of France), Jean de Menthon, Philibert de Gilly and Louise de Montmorency, wife o
2 CONC f Gaspard I de Coligny. Their only daughter and heir Jacqueline was born in Paris on 16 February 1541 and grew up in the Louvre until she was six.
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice was Maid of Honour to Queen Eleanor of Habsburg (1498-1558), sister of Emperor Charles V. Eleanor remarried in 1530 to Francis I of France and moved her Spanish courtiers and ladies in waiting into the Louvre Palace - one
2 CONC  of them was Beatrice. When Francis I died Eleanor took refuge in the Spanish Netherlands, home of her sister Mary of Hungary. Béatrix and Jacqueline went with her. Jacqueline remained in the Royal Court in Brussels until she was 
2 CONC sixteen, at which age she was chosen to be Maid of Honour to Princess Marguerite of France (1523-1574), Henry II's sister. Jacqueline returned to the Louvre in 1557, whilst her mother moved to the Château de Saint-André at Briord 
2 CONC in Bugey.
2 CONT
2 CONT C.Smith
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://pictura-prints.com/product/jacqueline-de-montbel-dentremont-portrait-p-79-la-comtesse-damtremont-lord-gower-after-clouet-1875/
2 CONT
2 CONT From: ‘Three Hundred French Portraits representing Personages of the Courts of Francis I , Henry II , and Francis II , by Clouet’, by Lord Ronald Gower, after the originals when they were at Castle Howard, Yorkshire. Published in 
2 CONC London 1875. First edition
2 CONT
2 CONT This scarce original antique print possibly shows a portrait of Jacqueline de Montbel d’Autremont (16 February 1541 – 17 December 1599), a French noblewoman or her mother Donna Beatrix Pacheco, Countess d’Autremont, lady-in-waitin
2 CONC g to Queen Eleanor. Auto-lithographed from the originals at Castle Howard, Yorkshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://pictura-prints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/07/pcom202.jpg}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
