1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Juana Porcallo de la Cerda ''' born about 1534 at Mazapil, Naucalpan, Mexico City, New Spain, died about 1581 at Saltillo, Coahuila, New Spain
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: don Diego de Montemayor, governor of Nuevo León.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juana and Diego de Montemayor had the following child:
2 CONT #Estefanía de Montemayor y Porcayo de la Cerda
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Juana Porcallo y de la Cerda was murdered by her husband, Diego de Montemayor, after discovering that she had been having carnal relations with Alberto del Canto. This was the same Alberto del Canto who later married their daughte
2 CONC r Estefania.
2 CONT
2 CONT Juana was the daughter of Vasco de Porcayo and Maria de la Cerda.
2 CONT
