2 CONT Name: Juana de Ulloa
2 CONT Gender: Female
2 CONT Birth: estimated between 1550 and 1576
2 CONT Parents (claimed): Pedro de Ulloa, II Marqués de la Mota, and Mariana de Ulloa
2 CONT Husband: Alonso Coronado y Maldonado, Oidor de la Audiencia en Guatemala
2 CONT Children: Luis Barba de Coronado; Capitán Juan de Coronado; Alonso de Coronado y Ulloa, Gobernador de la Provincia de Veraguas
2 CONT Siblings (claimed): Mariana de Ulloa; Luis de Ulloa y Quiñones, III Marqués de la Mota
2 CONT Source citations on profile: None
2 CONT Problem: Juana Does Not Appear in Any Spanish Source for the Marqueses de la Mota
2 CONT The documented children of Pedro de Ulloa and Mariana de Ulloa y Tavera
2 CONT
2 CONT Multiple independent Spanish sources document the children of Pedro de Ulloa (consort of the II Marquesa de la Mota) and Mariana de Ulloa y Tavera (II Marquesa de la Mota). They consistently name only two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Luis de Ulloa y Quiñones — III Marqués de la Mota, Caballero de Alcántara. Married Francisca de Zúñiga (died 1633), VIII Condesa de Nieva.
2 CONT Marina de Ulloa — married Antonio Francisco de Fonseca y Toledo, I Marqués de Villanueva de Valdueza.
2 CONT
2 CONT No daughter named Juana appears in any of these sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources consulted
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Wikipedia — "Marquesado de la Mota" (Spanish) URL: https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marquesado_de_la_Mota
2 CONT
2 CONT States the succession as:
2 CONT
2 CONT Rodrigo de Ulloa Toledo y Quiñones (died 1591), I Marqués de la Mota, married Marina Pardo Tavera y Saavedra (died 1582).
2 CONT Succeeded by his daughter: Mariana de Ulloa y Tavera, II Marquesa de la Mota, who married Pedro de Ulloa (her uncle).
2 CONT Succeeded by: Luis de Ulloa y Quiñones, III Marqués de la Mota.
2 CONT
2 CONT No other children of Pedro and Mariana are named in the succession record.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Heraldic study of the Mota del Marqués (Valladolid) URL: http://ptorrijos.blogspot.com/2011/10/escudo-en-la-mota-del-marques.html
2 CONT
2 CONT States: "Mariana de Ulloa y Tavera, II marquesa de la Mota. Casó con su tío carnal Pedro de Ulloa, citado antes, hermano de su padre. Padres de Luis de Ulloa y Ulloa, que sigue, y de Marina de Ulloa, casada con Antonio Francisco d
2 CONC e Fonseca y Toledo."
2 CONT
2 CONT Only two children named: Luis and Marina. No Juana.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Genealog.cl — Familia Ulloa URL: https://www.genealog.cl/Chile/U/Ulloa/
2 CONT
2 CONT Compiles the Ulloa genealogy from multiple sources including Salazar y Castro (1745), Wikipedia, Geni, and other references. Lists Pedro de Ulloa's marriage to Mariana de Ulloa y Tavera (his niece, II Marquesa). Records descendant
2 CONC s through Luis (III Marqués) and Marina. No Juana listed among children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. "Linaje Ulloa" — comprehensive genealogical study URL: http://www.royalrurikovich.com/images/genealogy/ullloa.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT Traces the Ulloa lineage through the Señores and Marqueses de la Mota. Lists Pedro and Mariana's children as Luis and Marina only. The succession continues through Luis to the IV Marqués and eventually passes to the Condes de Ayal
2 CONC a and then the Duques de Alba. No Juana appears.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Colonial Side: What Is Actually Documented
2 CONT Alonso de Coronado y Ulloa, Gobernador de Veraguas
2 CONT
2 CONT The Wikipedia article on his son, Alonso Coronado de Ulloa y Rengel (born Panamá 1613, died Lima 1670), states:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sus padres fueron los criollos centroamericanos Alonso Coronado y Ulloa, gobernador de la provincia de Veraguas, y Ana Rengel Palomeque."
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Alberto Tauro del Pino, Enciclopedia Ilustrada del Perú. URL: https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alonso_Coronado_y_Ulloa
2 CONT
2 CONT Key point: The parents are described as criollos centroamericanos — people born in the Americas of Spanish descent. This is consistent with a family already established in Central America, not with a daughter of a Castilian marqué
2 CONC s recently arrived from Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Coronado family in Central America
2 CONT
2 CONT The Vázquez de Coronado family is well-documented in Central American colonial history. The most famous member, Juan Vázquez de Coronado (conquistador of Costa Rica), was the illegitimate son of Gonzalo Vásquez de Coronado y Luján
2 CONC , VI Lord of Coquilla, from Salamanca. The family's presence in Central America dates to the mid-16th century. The "Ulloa" surname in the family may derive from:
2 CONT
2 CONT A genuine but lesser branch of the Ulloa family (not the Marqueses de la Mota)
2 CONT A maternal connection to an Ulloa family in the Salamanca/Toro region (where both Coronados and Ulloas were prominent) that was later inflated to the marquesado
2 CONT A colonial-era claim designed to enhance social standing
2 CONT Analysis: Pattern of Unverified Colonial-to-Spanish Connections
2 CONT
2 CONT This profile follows a pattern observed in other Geni entries for colonial Guatemalan families:
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by Guatemalan researchers working from colonial family traditions and local records
2 CONT No source citations provided for the Spanish parentage claim
2 CONT Bridge node characteristics: no birth date, no death date, no biographical detail — only a name and links connecting a colonial family to Spanish nobility
2 CONT Not corroborated by Spanish sources: the claimed parent (Pedro de Ulloa, II Marqués de la Mota) has well-documented children in multiple Spanish genealogical sources, and the claimed daughter does not appear among them
2 CONT Colonial incentive to claim noble descent: limpieza de sangre requirements, tax exemptions (hidalguía), access to government offices, and marriage prospects all created strong incentives to claim connections to known Spanish noble
2 CONC  houses
2 CONT Comparison with similar case: Esteban Fernández de Córdoba
2 CONT
2 CONT The same pattern appears in the profile of Esteban Fernández de Córdoba (ID: 6000000001265910510), who is listed as a son of Antonio Fernández de Córdoba y Cardona, V Duke of Sessa — despite Esteban not appearing in any Spanish so
2 CONC urce listing Antonio's twelve documented children. Like Juana, Esteban's profile was created by researchers working from Guatemalan colonial records and lacks source citations for the Spanish connection.
2 CONT
2 CONT Recommendations
2 CONT Add a note to Juana de Ulloa's profile stating that her claimed parentage (daughter of Pedro de Ulloa, II Marqués de la Mota) is not supported by any Spanish genealogical source. The documented children of Pedro and Mariana are Lu
2 CONC is (III Marqués) and Marina only.
2 CONT Remove or flag the parent links to Pedro de Ulloa, II Marqués de la Mota, and Mariana de Ulloa y Tavera, II Marquesa, until a primary source (baptismal record, testament, probanza) is produced confirming the relationship.
2 CONT Retain the link downward to Alonso de Coronado y Ulloa, Gobernador de Veraguas, as his mother is documented as carrying the Ulloa surname in colonial sources. The Ulloa connection may be genuine through a different, lesser branch 
2 CONC of the family.
2 CONT Note the "criollo" designation: Alonso de Coronado y Ulloa (the governor) is described as a "criollo centroamericano" in published sources, suggesting his parents were born in the Americas, not recently arrived from Spain.
2 CONT Request sources from profile managers: The profile was created in 2009 without citations. The managers (Vásquez Alburez, Gálvez Alburez, Barrios Pernillo) should be asked to provide documentary evidence for the claimed parentage.
2 CONT Sources Cited in This Document
2 CONT Wikipedia (Spanish): "Marquesado de la Mota" — https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marquesado_de_la_Mota
2 CONT Wikipedia (Spanish): "Alonso Coronado y Ulloa" — https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alonso_Coronado_y_Ulloa
2 CONT Wikipedia (English): "María de Ulloa" — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/María_de_Ulloa
2 CONT Wikipedia (English): "Juan Vázquez de Coronado" — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juan_Vázquez_de_Coronado
2 CONT Heraldic study, Mota del Marqués — http://ptorrijos.blogspot.com/2011/10/escudo-en-la-mota-del-marques.html
2 CONT Genealog.cl, Familia Ulloa — https://www.genealog.cl/Chile/U/Ulloa/
2 CONT Linaje Ulloa (genealogical study) — http://www.royalrurikovich.com/images/genealogy/ullloa.pdf
2 CONT Alberto Tauro del Pino, Enciclopedia Ilustrada del Perú
