1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alonso Fajardo de Tenza was the Governor-General of the Philippines, from July 3, 1618 to July 23, 1624, his death. He successfully defended the territory against the invading Dutch forces in 1618. He is said to ha
2 CONC ve died from melancholy. He killed his cheating wife and her lover. The lover’s house was torn down and he ordered that the spot remain vacant. Tamarind trees were planted to remind all of love gone “sour”. The location is called 
2 CONC Plaza Sampalucan along General Luna Street in Intramuros, Manila. For full biography, see the Spanish-language section.
