1 NOTE {geni:about_me} At the inquest on the “purity of blood” of Francisco Avendaño required for his entry to the university, sworn witnesses testified that “both lines come from the oldest and most distinguished families of Cumaná and 
2 CONC Margarita, in whose republics, since they were counted among the very first settlers and conquistadores, they have held the most important ecclesiastic, political, as well as military positions, for they were always known as true 
2 CONC Christians, free from mixture with evil races, and were never affronted publicly. Besides, they were noble hidalgos, originally from Vizcaya and descendants from the manorial homes of their respective surnames, which may be found 
2 CONC in the records of the Lords of Vizcaya.”
